Front-end pipeline stress (NOP)
===============================

Part of HW_Specific: tests that stress one hardware resource, to study how
interference on it shows up in other partitions. The sizes come from
BENCH_TOOLS/arch_config.h (cache and TLB geometry of the target).

What it tests
-------------

Interference on the front end of the pipeline (fetch and decode), with NOPs
only.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Every 10 ms executes 3 million NOPs (10000 blocks of 300 inline NOP
instructions).

Expected output
---------------

"3000000 NOP DONE" periodically.

Notes
-----

Under QEMU emulation 3 million NOPs can take longer than the 10 ms budget, and
the partition is restarted for a missed deadline.

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/PIPELINE/FRONT_PIPE_NOP/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/PIPELINE/FRONT_PIPE_NOP/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
